Third-party materials bundled in this repository:

* vendor/gpui-base — a patched copy of Longbridge's gpui-base, Apache-2.0
  (vendor/gpui-base/LICENSE-APACHE).
* crates/trek-assets/assets/file-icons — Catppuccin file icons, MIT
  (crates/trek-assets/assets/file-icons/LICENSE).
* crates/trek-assets/assets/fonts — Inter (The Inter Project Authors) and JetBrains Mono
  (The JetBrains Mono Project Authors), both under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
  (OFL-Inter.txt and OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt in that folder), and the KaTeX fonts
  (Design Science, Inc. and Khan Academy), seven of them modified and renamed TrekMath,
  SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL-KaTeX.txt), and Spectral (The Spectral Project Authors),
  SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL-Spectral.txt), the serif Trek themes may set text in.
  The iPhone app bundles the same Inter, JetBrains Mono, KaTeX and Spectral fonts, with their
  licences, in ios/Trek/Resources/Fonts.
* ios/Trek/Backgrounds.xcassets — the background art of crates/trek-assets/assets/backgrounds
  cut to a phone's shape (ios/scripts/backgrounds.py); the paintings are public domain, as
  assets/backgrounds/SOURCES.md says.
* crates/trek-math/src/tables.rs — glyph metrics and the math symbol table from
  KaTeX (Khan Academy and other contributors), MIT; the layout rules in
  crates/trek-math/src/layout.rs follow KaTeX's implementation of TeX's
  (crates/trek-math/LICENSE-KaTeX).
* crates/trek-mcp/src/desktop/skylight.rs — the recipe for input to a window in the
  background (the window server's event records and event fields) follows the findings of
  cua-driver (Cua AI, github.com/trycua/cua), MIT.
* crates/trek-phone/src/hid.rs and crates/trek-phone/helper/main.swift — the HID report map
  (an absolute pointer whose presses go through a second, relative mouse) and the HID over
  GATT service layout follow iphone-use (NewWave AI, github.com/xhoantran/iphone-use), MIT.
  The iPhone's own services are reached through the idevice crate (Jackson Coxson), MIT.
* ios/TrekDriver/Driver/Capture.swift and Stream.swift — asking XCTest's daemon for the screen
  as a JPEG and serving it as an MJPEG stream follows WebDriverAgent (Appium and Facebook,
  github.com/appium/WebDriverAgent: FBScreenshot.m, FBMjpegServer.m), BSD-3-Clause; no code of
  theirs is included. The element outline with refs for agents (crates/trek-mcp/src/phone.rs,
  ios/TrekDriver/Driver/Elements.swift) follows the shape of terminal-phone (Govijr,
  github.com/govijr/terminal-phone), MIT.
* Dictation on Windows (crates/trek-dictate/src/windows), and watch_video's transcripts there
  (crates/trek-mcp), run whisper.cpp (The ggml authors, github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp), MIT,
  compiled into Trek through the whisper-rs crates (Unlicense). vendor/whisper-rs-sys is a
  patched copy of whisper-rs-sys 0.15 with the whisper.cpp sources it carries, their GPU
  backends left out (vendor/whisper-rs-sys/whisper.cpp/LICENSE). The speech model dictation
  downloads the first time the mic is used is OpenAI's Whisper base model
  (github.com/openai/whisper), MIT, as whisper.cpp publishes it.
* Agent and provider logos under crates/trek-assets/assets/logos,
  ios/Trek/Assets.xcassets/Logos and site/remote/logos are trademarks of their respective owners
  (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Microsoft/GitHub, xAI, Cursor, Factory, DeepSeek,
  Moonshot, Alibaba, Ollama, LM Studio, OpenRouter, Mistral, Groq, Cognition,
  Sourcegraph, SST, Pi, and others). They are included solely to identify which
  agent or provider a thread or setting uses; no endorsement or affiliation is
  implied, and Trek claims no rights in those marks. Trademark holders may
  request removal via a GitHub issue.
  The PNG files themselves were added on 2 October 2026 with no record of where each was taken
  from; the one-colour glyphs below are the ones whose source is known.
* site/remote/vendor — the web remote's libraries, as their authors publish them: Preact
  (Jason Miller), MIT; htm (Google), Apache-2.0; marked (Christopher Jeffrey and contributors), MIT;
  DOMPurify (Cure53 and contributors), Apache-2.0 or MPL-2.0; and KaTeX (Khan Academy and other
  contributors), MIT, with its fonts under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Each licence is beside
  it in that folder.
* site/assets/fonts — the website's type: Bricolage Grotesque (The Bricolage Grotesque Project
  Authors) and Hanken Grotesk (The Hanken Grotesk Project Authors), both SIL Open Font License 1.1,
  as the @fontsource-variable packages publish them, and a Latin subset of JetBrains Mono (see
  above). Each licence is beside its font as OFL-*.txt.
* site/assets/img/backdrop — the website's two photographs, graded by script/site/make_backdrops.py:
  "Dried grass field under blue sky during daytime" by Chris Mongeau
  (unsplash.com/photos/ZRdSZeVKBaE) and "The sun is setting over a field of tall grass" by
  Johannes Plenio (unsplash.com/photos/X7RUQSjQv0k), both under the Unsplash License.
* ios/Trek/Assets.xcassets/Glyphs — one-colour agent marks from Lobe Icons
  (@lobehub/icons-static-svg 1.95.1), MIT, with each path's arc flags written out; the marks
  themselves belong to their owners, as the logos above do.
* crates/trek-assets/assets/katex — KaTeX 0.16.11 (Khan Academy and other contributors), as the
  npm package publishes it (katex.min.js, contrib/auto-render.min.js, katex.min.css and the
  woff2 fonts), MIT (LICENSE in that folder) with the fonts under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
  (OFL-KaTeX.txt). Study question cards draw their formulas with it, served from the app itself.
* ios/Trek/Assets.xcassets/Cards — the glyphs on the iPhone's cards (git merge, pull request,
  rocket, workflow and the like) are Lucide icons (Lucide Icons and Contributors), ISC (the
  licence text is docs/assets/icons/features/LICENSE), with their stroke widths changed.
* Made for Trek and under its licence, with nothing taken from elsewhere: the drawings in
  plugins/examples/*/art; the four sounds in plugins/examples/soft-sounds/sounds, which were
  synthesised for that plugin (plain tones with a fading tail, each peaking at the same level,
  added 17 November 2026); crates/trek-assets/assets/icons/hub.svg; assets/dmg/background.svg
  (drawn by script/dmg-background.sh); and the demo recordings and screenshots under ios/screenshots,
  site/assets/img/features and site/assets/img/window-*, which are captures of Trek itself.
* Model metadata (context windows, pricing) is sourced from models.dev.
* docs/assets/icons/features — Lucide icons (Lucide Icons and Contributors), ISC
  (docs/assets/icons/features/LICENSE), recoloured. docs/assets/icons/tech and
  docs/assets/icons/platforms draw Simple Icons glyphs (CC0 1.0) and a plain four-pane
  window; the marks they show
  (Rust, Swift, SQLite, Apple, Windows) belong to their owners.
